9. Quality bar
A tool is done when it works with real inputs and edge cases; has loading, empty, error, offline and success states; remembers its last settings; offers copy, save, share and Send to…; has keyboard and screen-reader support; shows requirement and privacy chips honestly; ships a help sheet; has tests for its logic; and looks like it belongs to its chapter.
Never: mock data, fake progress, dead buttons, lorem ipsum, invented sensor readings, invented statistics or citations, hard-coded tax or interest rates, silent network calls, secrets in code, tools that only work in the AI Studio preview, files over 400 lines, a component that ignores the tokens.
